<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hoshiarpur district</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hoshiarpur district lies in the Indian state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beas">Beas</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sutlej-river">Sutlej</a> at the foot of the Shivalik hills, with its headquarters at the city of Hoshiarpur. It formed part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bist-doab">Jalandhar Doab</a>, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> annexed from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> kingdom in 1846. Several small <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> hill states, such as Datarpur, lay within its area.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hoshiarpur-district.jpg" alt="Hoshiarpur district" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Karantsingh · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bajwara_Fort_Hoshiarpur.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
